      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (50%):</strong> The dominant case — talks frozen, Hormuz near-closed (F3 at 20%), no comprehensive deal (F4 at 20%), Iran enforcing fee-based access regime indefinitely while both sides avoid full resumption of hostilities.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (15%):</strong> Conditional on F2 resolving YES (Iran–US structured talks resume) and F3 making progress toward 10 transits/day, requiring an Oman-brokered interim transit agreement that the US tolerates.</p>
