  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN (descriptive, ~200 words) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>IRNA and Tasnim on August 25–26 framed Iran's Hormuz access regime as a postwar sovereign right rather than a temporary wartime measure, quoting unnamed Foreign Ministry officials to the effect that the strait's legal status has been permanently altered. This framing treats the vessel blacklist — 46 ships threatened with fines, detention or seizure — as the baseline for any future transit arrangement, not a concession to be bargained away. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span></p>
      <p>IRIB evening broadcasts on August 25 covered the blacklist publication with IRGC commentary describing violating vessels as having "already faced consequences," a claim not independently confirmed by TIER1 sources. Press TV on August 26 framed Trump's Oman threat (August 17) as a sign of US desperation and the MOU expiry as a US failure to fulfill commitments — a standard inversion of the US position. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
      <p>Kayhan's August 25 editorial calling for enrichment above 60% as a "legitimate response" to renewed sanctions represents one measurable end of an internal debate; Fars News Agency's more cautious coverage of the same day's nuclear file, emphasizing IAEA monitoring continuity, represents another. Neither AEOI nor the Supreme Leader office has issued an operational statement. → moved <span class="cite">F5</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

